WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:15.719
Zann exclaimed.

2
00:00:15.739 --> 00:00:18.260
"You oversized swamp rat!

3
00:00:18.761 --> 00:00:19.881
I'll get you for that."

4
00:00:20.742 --> 00:00:22.803
Picking up a rock, he tossed it at the dragon.

5
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:25.725
Zing ducked the rock, chattering in annoyance.

6
00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:27.265
Zann grinned.

7
00:00:27.285 --> 00:00:28.606
"What do you expect?"

8
00:00:28.926 --> 00:00:29.267
he said.

9
00:00:29.287 --> 00:00:31.628
"You just tried to roast me!"

10
00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:36.615
The dragon hopped down from the roof, not bothering to unfurl its leathery wings.

11
00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.617
It landed beside Zann with a thump.

12
00:00:40.258 --> 00:00:42.079
He bent to scratch its pointy little head.

13
00:00:42.099 --> 00:00:43.500
"Did you eat yet?"

14
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:44.421
he asked.

15
00:00:44.441 --> 00:00:45.822
"Let's go inside.

16
00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:50.185
I'll conjure up some food for you as soon as I tell Boz about the warning."

17
00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:52.526
The dragon chirped agreeably.

18
00:00:53.147 --> 00:00:57.710
Many people kept dragons as pets, but fire whistlers like Zing weren’t very popular.

19
00:00:58.951 --> 00:01:03.393
The breed was too active, too independent, and a little too unpredictable.

20
00:01:04.053 --> 00:01:07.654
Besides, most people didn't like dealing with a pet that could set you on fire.

21
00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:09.995
But Zing was perfect for Zann.

22
00:01:10.255 --> 00:01:11.455
They spent hours together.

23
00:01:12.095 --> 00:01:14.956
Their favorite game was to lie in wait and attack each other.

24
00:01:15.756 --> 00:01:19.537
Zann reached for his schoolbag, which he'd dropped during Zing's surprise attack.

25
00:01:20.718 --> 00:01:24.519
"You'd better sleep with one eye open," he told the dragon jokingly.

26
00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:29.420
Dragons couldn't talk, but the smarter ones could understand some human speech.

27
00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:35.588
"Because when you least expect it, I'm going to grab you and feed you to the water blobs."

28
00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:40.891
Zing hissed playfully, sending out a spurt of flame that Zann dodged easily.

29
00:01:41.611 --> 00:01:43.893
He laughed, glancing around for another rock.

30
00:01:45.294 --> 00:01:47.575
Before he could find one, the door flew open.

31
00:01:47.595 --> 00:01:53.919
"Get in here," Boz ordered, the tip of his long, pointy nose quivering as it always did when

32
00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:55.220
he was worked up about something.

33
00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:01.062
Zann's grandfather was clutching the tattered diary in which he recorded everything important that happened to him.

34
00:02:01.082 --> 00:02:03.182
"I need to talk to you."

35
00:02:04.122 --> 00:02:06.823
Zann guessed that Boz had already heard about the message.

36
00:02:06.843 --> 00:02:08.424
"I'm coming," he said.

37
00:02:09.684 --> 00:02:12.705
Like the outside, the inside of their house rarely changed.

38
00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:19.247
Half the furniture was boring and utilitarian, transported there by Boz from his old home in First City.

39
00:02:19.927 --> 00:02:25.069
The rest was cool stuff that Zann's parents had conjured, mostly based on interesting things they had seen

40
00:02:25.089 --> 00:02:30.530
in their travels: a statue of a frightening beast from the slopes of Mount Mystery, replicas of the

41
00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:37.452
low-slung chairs used by nomadic settlers way out on the Far Frontier, and an exotic-looking lamp from some

42
00:02:37.492 --> 00:02:38.633
other, faraway world.

43
00:02:39.713 --> 00:02:41.134
That lamp was Zann's favorite.

44
00:02:41.714 --> 00:02:47.135
He paused beside it, resting a hand on its lumpy surface and glancing at the framed blink images

45
00:02:47.215 --> 00:02:48.736
of his family hanging on the walls.

46
00:02:49.448 --> 00:02:53.069
Could his parents be trapped in some mysterious other world even now?

47
00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:56.210
Could they still be alive despite what most people thought?

48
00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.451
Zing scampered over to grab a scorched chew toy.

49
00:03:00.071 --> 00:03:01.191
Boz stared at Zann.

50
00:03:02.252 --> 00:03:03.832
His large brown eyes were troubled.

51
00:03:03.852 --> 00:03:08.393
"I'm glad you're home," he said, setting his diary on the table.

52
00:03:08.413 --> 00:03:11.734
"I thought about going down to your school to get you.

53
00:03:12.554 --> 00:03:14.735
Have you heard about the warning from the palace?"

54
00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.175
Zann nodded.

55
00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.956
"An echo crow came to school.

56
00:03:18.784 --> 00:03:20.545
The message sounded pretty weird.

57
00:03:21.366 --> 00:03:23.848
Why would Reds suddenly start disappearing?"

58
00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.909
"I don't know."

59
00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:28.771
Boz rubbed his nose to stop it from quivering.

60
00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:33.234
"I've sent messages to a few friends to see if any of them know anything.

61
00:03:33.915 --> 00:03:35.276
But they haven't responded.

62
00:03:36.076 --> 00:03:39.759
That worries me, especially since they're all Reds."

63
00:03:40.639 --> 00:03:44.402
He tapped one finger against another, and several message moths appeared.

64
00:03:45.063 --> 00:03:48.616
Boz focused his gaze on one, muttering a message under his breath.

65
00:03:49.657 --> 00:03:53.918
As he spoke, tiny words etched themselves onto the moth's powdery wings.

66
00:03:54.658 --> 00:03:56.219
Zann couldn't help being impressed.

67
00:03:56.999 --> 00:03:59.500
Most people had to inscribe message moths by hand.

68
00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.721
Only a few people had the focus to do it by eye.

69
00:04:03.381 --> 00:04:08.342
Sometimes it was easy to forget that his grandfather had been one of the most powerful Magic Masters

70
00:04:08.382 --> 00:04:08.902
in the kingdom.

71
00:04:09.643 --> 00:04:13.964
Zann wondered if he himself would ever develop that kind of control over his own powers.

72
00:04:14.996 --> 00:04:18.617
He realized Boz had finished inscribing the message moths and was talking again.

73
00:04:19.317 --> 00:04:22.018
He'd just said something about wanting Zann to stay at home.

74
00:04:22.038 --> 00:04:24.099
"What?" Zann blurted out.

75
00:04:24.119 --> 00:04:27.500
"But I told Darb I'd meet him at the swamp after dinner!"

76
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.160
"Sorry, Zann.

77
00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.921
We need to be careful until I find out what we're dealing with."

78
00:04:33.682 --> 00:04:36.622
Boz waved a hand to send the moths fluttering out the window.

79
00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:39.423
"I can't risk you wandering off."

80
00:04:39.443 --> 00:04:41.644
"What's the difference?

81
00:04:42.108 --> 00:04:45.489
It's not like anything ever happens way out here in Swamp Bottom.

82
00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:50.752
I still don't know why you decided to move to this place after Mom and Dad disappeared.

83
00:04:51.572 --> 00:04:56.074
We'll never find out what happened to them while we're stuck out here in this boring old backwater."

84
00:04:56.094 --> 00:05:00.216
"I'll make dinner in an hour" was all Boz said.

85
00:05:00.236 --> 00:05:02.837
"You'd better get started on your homework."

86
00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:05.518
"Typical," thought Zann.

87
00:05:06.258 --> 00:05:09.179
Boz never wanted to talk about what had happened to Zann's parents.

88
00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:10.740
Zann didn't get it.

89
00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.063
Didn't Boz want to find them if they were still out there somewhere?

90
00:05:14.083 --> 00:05:18.046
"Come here, Zing," he called.

91
00:05:18.066 --> 00:05:23.952
"Dinnertime." He rubbed his fingers together and pointed at the dragon's food dish.

92
00:05:24.492 --> 00:05:27.475
A big helping of green, slimy dragon mush appeared.

93
00:05:28.435 --> 00:05:30.117
Zing flapped his wings in thanks.

94
00:05:30.858 --> 00:05:34.060
Then he shot out a flicker of flame and instantly cooked the mush.

95
00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.884
It smelled disgusting, but the dragon slurped it up eagerly.

96
00:05:38.588 --> 00:05:41.230
Zann turned around and realized Boz was watching him.

97
00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.473
"I'm not trying to ruin your fun, Zann," Boz said.

98
00:05:45.493 --> 00:05:47.534
"I just want to protect you."

99
00:05:47.554 --> 00:05:49.075
"I know."

100
00:05:49.576 --> 00:05:51.457
Zann felt guilty for his earlier thoughts.

101
00:05:51.477 --> 00:05:52.918
"It's okay."

102
00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.662
But after dinner Zann felt much too restless to sit in his room and study.

103
00:06:00.323 --> 00:06:02.224
He checked to make sure Boz wasn't nearby.

104
00:06:04.446 --> 00:06:07.588
Then he rubbed his hands together and zapped himself out of the house.
